WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:08.952
Forge turns this Python expression into a native kernel. Nine elements go in, and both execution plans return the same float32 values.

00:00:09.752 --> 00:00:17.993
The unfused plan runs add, multiply, and square root in separate loops. Two temporary arrays carry values between those passes.

00:00:18.793 --> 00:00:26.257
The fused plan performs all three operations inside one loop. The intermediate values stay in registers until the result is written.

00:00:27.057 --> 00:00:39.692
In the isolated Linux probe, the unfused workspace needs sixty-four MiB of scratch. For the separate sixty-five thousand five hundred thirty-six element case, compare the warm native A V X two medians.
